From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] engine: bare_app: the gamepad preset of the device

bare_app names a preset of gamepad_presets/ for the device it runs on in
XASH3D_GAMEPAD_PRESET (the GO Advance: odroid_go_advance, its one stick
turns the view and the d-pad walks). The engine applies it once, while
the gamepad's keys and axes are still the defaults, as it does for the
known SDL controllers; the menu's Gamepad page picks another one.

--- a/engine/platform/bare_app/bare_app.c
+++ b/engine/platform/bare_app/bare_app.c
@@ -874,9 +874,20 @@
 	ba.mouse_grab = enable;
 }
 
+/*
+==============
+Platform_JoyInit
+
+The gamepad is the device's own: its preset (gamepad_presets/<name>.cfg) is
+what bare_app names in XASH3D_GAMEPAD_PRESET, applied once while nobody
+has changed the gamepad's keys, as with SDL's known controllers
+==============
+*/
 int Platform_JoyInit( void )
 {
-	Joy_SetCapabilities( false, 0, NULL );
+	const char *preset = getenv( "XASH3D_GAMEPAD_PRESET" );
+
+	Joy_SetCapabilities( false, 0, COM_StringEmptyOrNULL( preset ) ? NULL : preset );
 	return 1;
 }
 
